      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A SQL Client\nEach read, create, update and delete of a\nresource first opens a connection to the\nserver ([connect code](https://github.com/cyri\nlgdn/terraform-provider-postgresql/blob/v1.27.\n0/postgresql/helpers.go#L14-L36)). The\nprovider settings say where and how ([provider\nsettings](https://github.com/cyrilgdn/terrafor\nm-provider-postgresql/blob/v1.27.0/website/doc\ns/index.html.markdown#L141-L188)):\n\n- `host`, `port`, `database`, `username` and\n`password`, or the environment variables\n`PGHOST`, `PGPORT`, `PGDATABASE`, `PGUSER` and\n`PGPASSWORD`.\n- `sslmode`, whose default `require` encrypts\nthe connection but does not check the server\ncertificate. `verify-full` checks it.\n- `superuser`, which must be `false` on RDS.\n- `expected_version`. Without it, each new\nconnection runs `SELECT VERSION()` to detect\nthe server's features ([config code](https://g\nithub.com/cyrilgdn/terraform-provider-postgres\nql/blob/v1.27.0/postgresql/config.go#L318-L327\n)).\n\nSo the machine that runs the plan must reach\nthe server's port 5432 and log in with a valid\npassword.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-bef2980b4c40",
      "originalText": "A SQL Client\nEach read, create, update and delete of a resource first opens a connection to the server ([connect code](https://github.com/cyrilgdn/terraform-provider-postgresql/blob/v1.27.0/postgresql/helpers.go#L14-L36)). The provider settings say where and how ([provider settings](https://github.com/cyrilgdn/terraform-provider-postgresql/blob/v1.27.0/website/docs/index.html.markdown#L141-L188)):\n\n- `host`, `port`, `database`, `username` and `password`, or the environment variables `PGHOST`, `PGPORT`, `PGDATABASE`, `PGUSER` and `PGPASSWORD`.\n- `sslmode`, whose default `require` encrypts the connection but does not check the server certificate. `verify-full` checks it.\n- `superuser`, which must be `false` on RDS.\n- `expected_version`. Without it, each new connection runs `SELECT VERSION()` to detect the server's features ([config code](https://github.com/cyrilgdn/terraform-provider-postgresql/blob/v1.27.0/postgresql/config.go#L318-L327)).\n\nSo the machine that runs the plan must reach the server's port 5432 and log in with a valid password.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "a-sql-client"
      }
    },
    {
