      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A Grant Owns Its Set\nOne `postgresql_grant` covers one combination\nof role, database, schema and object type,\nsuch as \"role `app`, tables in schema\n`public`\". On every create and update, it\nrevokes all privileges of that combination and\nthen grants its own list, in one transaction\n([grant code](https://github.com/cyrilgdn/terr\naform-provider-postgresql/blob/v1.27.0/postgre\nsql/resource_postgresql_grant.go#L194-L204)).\nSo any other grant on the same combination,\nmade by hand or by another resource,\ndisappears at the next update.\n\n`objects = []` means all objects of that type\nthat exist at apply time. A refresh checks\nevery one of them, so a table created later\nshows as a difference.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-ab4e0bab5b80",
      "originalText": "A Grant Owns Its Set\nOne `postgresql_grant` covers one combination of role, database, schema and object type, such as \"role `app`, tables in schema `public`\". On every create and update, it revokes all privileges of that combination and then grants its own list, in one transaction ([grant code](https://github.com/cyrilgdn/terraform-provider-postgresql/blob/v1.27.0/postgresql/resource_postgresql_grant.go#L194-L204)). So any other grant on the same combination, made by hand or by another resource, disappears at the next update.\n\n`objects = []` means all objects of that type that exist at apply time. A refresh checks every one of them, so a table created later shows as a difference.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "a-grant-owns-its-set"
      }
    },
