      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 2657931197,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-2ddb7537c012",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1321.2,
      "y": 1940.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 394.8,
      "height": 560.0,
      "seed": 567344,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Where to Look First\nRead a PostgreSQL configuration in this order:\n\n1. `required_providers` and the Terraform\nversion. Provider 1.24.0 is \"the first version\ncompatible with Postgresql 16\" ([v1.24.0](http\ns://github.com/cyrilgdn/terraform-provider-pos\ntgresql/releases/tag/v1.24.0)). The ephemeral\n`password_wo` arrived in 1.26.0 ([v1.26.0](htt\nps://github.com/cyrilgdn/terraform-provider-po\nstgresql/releases/tag/v1.26.0)) and needs\nTerraform 1.11.\n2. The `provider \"postgresql\"` block, or its\nabsence. Find where the host, user, password\nand `sslmode` come from, and whether\n`superuser = false` is set.\n3. The pipeline. Find how the runner reaches\nport 5432, and which credentials each stage\ngets.\n4. The environment inputs. Find which role is\nthe app's user and owner in each environment.\n5. `postgresql_role`: the password source,\n`ignore_changes`, and `skip_reassign_owned` or\n`skip_drop_role`.\n6. `postgresql_database`: the owner,\n`prevent_destroy`, and the arguments that\nforce a replacement.\n7. `postgresql_grant`: is the grantee also the\nowner, is `objects` empty, and do two\nresources cover one combination?\n8. `postgresql_default_privileges`: is `owner`\nthe role that creates the tables?",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-2ddb7537c012",
      "originalText": "Where to Look First\nRead a PostgreSQL configuration in this order:\n\n1. `required_providers` and the Terraform version. Provider 1.24.0 is \"the first version compatible with Postgresql 16\" ([v1.24.0](https://github.com/cyrilgdn/terraform-provider-postgresql/releases/tag/v1.24.0)). The ephemeral `password_wo` arrived in 1.26.0 ([v1.26.0](https://github.com/cyrilgdn/terraform-provider-postgresql/releases/tag/v1.26.0)) and needs Terraform 1.11.\n2. The `provider \"postgresql\"` block, or its absence. Find where the host, user, password and `sslmode` come from, and whether `superuser = false` is set.\n3. The pipeline. Find how the runner reaches port 5432, and which credentials each stage gets.\n4. The environment inputs. Find which role is the app's user and owner in each environment.\n5. `postgresql_role`: the password source, `ignore_changes`, and `skip_reassign_owned` or `skip_drop_role`.\n6. `postgresql_database`: the owner, `prevent_destroy`, and the arguments that force a replacement.\n7. `postgresql_grant`: is the grantee also the owner, is `objects` empty, and do two resources cover one combination?\n8. `postgresql_default_privileges`: is `owner` the role that creates the tables?",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "pg-where-to-look-first"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 2305279193,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "node-d2ca72066928",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
