      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 9013463850,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-d82fa53cd5d8",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1864.0,
      "y": 3417.5,
      "strokeColor": "#92400E",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 386.40000000000003,
      "height": 192.5,
      "seed": 673746,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Default Privileges Miss Objects\nA rule for future tables helps only when its\n`owner` is the role that really creates the\ntables. If migrations run as the app role, but\nthe rule names the Terraform admin, new tables\nget no privileges for the reader, and queries\nfail with \"permission denied\". The plan shows\nnothing, because the rule itself is unchanged.\nUse one rule for each role that creates\nobjects, and a grant for the tables that exist\nalready.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-d82fa53cd5d8",
      "originalText": "Default Privileges Miss Objects\nA rule for future tables helps only when its `owner` is the role that really creates the tables. If migrations run as the app role, but the rule names the Terraform admin, new tables get no privileges for the reader, and queries fail with \"permission denied\". The plan shows nothing, because the rule itself is unchanged. Use one rule for each role that creates objects, and a grant for the tables that exist already.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "default-privileges-miss-objects"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
