    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 3871511249,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-4a532f16afe1",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1864.0,
      "y": 4187.0,
      "strokeColor": "#92400E",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 394.8,
      "height": 210.0,
      "seed": 51278,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Passwords in State\nAll arguments of `postgresql_role`, including\nthe password, sit in the state in plain text\n([role doc](https://github.com/cyrilgdn/terraf\norm-provider-postgresql/blob/v1.27.0/website/d\nocs/r/postgresql_role.html.markdown#L24)). So\ndoes the master password of an RDS instance\nthat the AWS provider creates. `password_wo`\nkeeps a role password out of the state ([role \ndoc](https://github.com/cyrilgdn/terraform-pro\nvider-postgresql/blob/v1.27.0/website/docs/r/p\nostgresql_role.html.markdown#L27-L29)).",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-4a532f16afe1",
      "originalText": "Passwords in State\nAll arguments of `postgresql_role`, including the password, sit in the state in plain text ([role doc](https://github.com/cyrilgdn/terraform-provider-postgresql/blob/v1.27.0/website/docs/r/postgresql_role.html.markdown#L24)). So does the master password of an RDS instance that the AWS provider creates. `password_wo` keeps a role password out of the state ([role doc](https://github.com/cyrilgdn/terraform-provider-postgresql/blob/v1.27.0/website/docs/r/postgresql_role.html.markdown#L27-L29)).",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "pg-passwords-in-state"
      }
    },
